# /etc/restic/env — restic backup configuration (read by restic-backup.service)
# Set RESTIC_REPOSITORY to an S3/B2/MinIO/local repo. Leave empty until configured;
# the timer is NOT enabled by default so nothing runs until an operator opts in.
#
# Password management:
# Supply the repository password via systemd encrypted credentials (matching borgmatic):
#   systemd-creds encrypt - /etc/credstore.encrypted/restic.pw
# which is loaded by restic-backup.service via `LoadCredentialEncrypted=restic.pw`.
# Alternatively, set RESTIC_PASSWORD_FILE below to point to a mode-0600 password file.
RESTIC_REPOSITORY=
# RESTIC_PASSWORD_FILE=/etc/restic/password
# RESTIC_OPTIONS=
# BACKUP_PATHS="/etc /var /home"
